s10-10-p6 = realized (prose (cons "The initial state has \(p=0\), \(O=\varnothing\), \(U=\varnothing\), \(L=Q=[]\), so \(I_B\) holds for \(B\ge0\). The invariant-based reasoning follows the classical discipline of proving preservation over program transitions ([68](#ref-68)). Admission preserves \(I_B\) by its guard; a full fill moves \(q\) from \(O\) to \(p\), hence leaves \(R\) **unchanged**; cancellation removes a nonnegative outstanding summand; receive and stale handling change neither \(p\) nor \(O\). Therefore induction over finite traces constructs" (cons "\[" (cons "\mathsf{safe}_B:\prod_{\tau:\mathsf{FiniteRun}(F_B,s_0)}" (cons "R(p(\mathsf{last}(\tau)),O(\mathsf{last}(\tau)))\le B." (cons "\tag{10.T3}" (cons "\]" (cons "The state carries the separate invariant \(\operatorname{dom}(O)\subseteq U\). To prove that each order identifier appears **at most once** in the accepted-fill ledger, maintain simultaneously" (cons "\[" (cons "\begin{aligned}" (cons "J(O,U,L):={}&\mathsf{NoDup}(\mathsf{ids}(L))\\" (cons "&\times(\mathsf{set}(\mathsf{ids}(L))\subseteq U)\\" (cons "&\times(\mathsf{set}(\mathsf{ids}(L))\cap\operatorname{dom}(O)=\varnothing)." (cons "\end{aligned}" (cons "\tag{10.T4}" (cons "\]" (cons "The initial state satisfies \(J\). Admission adds an identifier outside \(U\), so it is neither in the ledger nor an existing open order. A fill removes an open identifier that, by the third conjunct, is absent from the ledger before appending it; the second conjunct follows from \(\operatorname{dom}(O)\subseteq U\). Cancellation shrinks the open domain, and receive/stale transitions leave these sets unchanged. Thus a *second* finite-trace induction establishes \(J\) and \(\mathsf{count}_L(i)\le1\). The risk bound alone does not establish ledger uniqueness: both properties require their own invariant components and preservation arguments." nil))))))))))))))))) (cons (cite gw-step-IB "gw-step-IB") (cons (cite gw-safe "gw-safe") (cons (cite gw-J "gw-J") (cons (cite gw-K "gw-K") (cons (cite gw-step-J "gw-step-J") (cons (cite gw-J-run "gw-J-run") (cons (cite gw-unique "gw-unique") nil)))))))
